INTERPRETATION NOTES
- Figure 1 separates monetary and time-related components of generalised cost.
- Figure 2 tests the sensitivity of generalised cost to alternative Values of Time.
- Figure 3 evaluates monetary-cost versus door-to-door-time trade-offs independently of VOT.
- Pareto efficiency does not imply overall superiority in comfort, safety, reliability or other unmodelled attributes.
- Private bicycle and private e-scooter are the Pareto-efficient modes under the current cost and travel-time assumptions.
